# The launcher's default file rules: project files a program on your host runs a command from
# when you start an agent in the project, commit, open it in an editor, enter its directory, or
# reopen it in a Dev Container. A session cannot change them at any depth, except inside
# node_modules (the last line). Build files, scripts and package.json stay writable, because you
# run those yourself.
#
# - A file is listed unless a command you run for another purpose rewrites it, the way
#   `npm install` rewrites package-lock.json, or its program asks you again when it changes, as
#   direnv does for .envrc (doc/file-rule-example/direnv/rule lists it).
# - A command meant to change a listed file, such as `pre-commit autoupdate`, `mise use` or
#   `claude mcp add --scope project`, runs on the host, as `--update` does for the agents.
# - Editors are assumed to run on the host. A project whose editor or agent maintains a listed
#   file in the sandbox adds a `writable` line for it to .ko-agent-sandbox/file/rule.
#
# The reasons, source by source: doc/file-rules.md, "Why these files".

# Agents on the host: hooks, helper commands and the MCP servers their project files name.
readonly .claude/settings.json          # Claude Code, Copilot CLI
readonly .claude/settings.local.json
readonly .claude/skills                 # Claude Code: hooks and !`command` lines
readonly .claude/agents                 # Claude Code, Copilot CLI
readonly .claude/commands
readonly .mcp.json                      # Claude Code, Copilot CLI
readonly .codex/config.toml             # Codex
readonly .gemini/settings.json          # Gemini CLI
readonly .github/hooks                  # Copilot CLI
readonly .github/copilot/settings.json
readonly .github/copilot/settings.local.json
readonly .github/mcp.json
readonly .github/lsp.json
readonly .github/extensions
readonly .github/agents
readonly .agents/hooks.json             # Antigravity
readonly .agents/mcp_config.json
readonly .agents/plugins
readonly .kiro/hooks                    # Kiro
readonly .kiro/agents
readonly .kiro/settings/mcp.json
readonly .opencode                      # OpenCode: plugins, tools and commands it loads
readonly opencode.json
readonly opencode.jsonc

# Git hook managers: the hook installed in .git runs what these name at each commit.
readonly .husky
readonly .pre-commit-config.yaml
readonly lefthook.*                     # .config/lefthook.* too: a name matches at any depth
readonly .lefthook.*
readonly lefthook-local.*
readonly .lefthook-local.*

# Editors: configuration a trusted folder runs.
readonly .vscode                        # VS Code, and Zed for its tasks and launch files
readonly *.code-workspace
readonly .vs                            # Visual Studio
readonly tasks.vs.json
readonly launch.vs.json
readonly .idea                          # IntelliJ IDEA
readonly .cursor/hooks.json             # Cursor
readonly .cursor/mcp.json
readonly .windsurf/hooks.json           # Windsurf
readonly .devin/hooks.json
readonly .zed                           # Zed

# Dev Containers: initializeCommand runs on the host.
readonly .devcontainer
readonly .devcontainer.json

# mise: [hooks] enter runs when you enter the directory, and a file stays trusted by path.
readonly mise.toml                      # .config/mise.toml too: a name matches at any depth
readonly .mise.toml
readonly mise.*.toml
readonly .mise.*.toml
readonly mise
readonly .mise
readonly .tool-versions                 # its templates can run commands
readonly .miserc.toml                   # which configuration files load
readonly .miserc.*.toml
readonly miserc.toml                    # .config/miserc.toml, without pinning every .config

# Last, so it decides inside node_modules: npm installs packages that carry listed names.
writable node_modules
